<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">San José, Costa Rica</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">San José is the capital and largest city of Costa Rica, in the Central Valley. Founded in the 18th century, it became capital in 1823 after a brief civil war in which its republicans defeated the conservative towns of Cartago and Heredia over joining <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>. It grew rich from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a> in the 19th century, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pact-of-union-1921">Pact of Union of Central America</a> was signed there in 1921.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/san-jose-costa-rica.jpg" alt="San José, Costa Rica" width="320" height="456" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alejandro Álvarez Taborda (Aleat88) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ciudad_de_San_Jos%C3%A9.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
